    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment": [
      {
        "@value": "Relationship between unit efficiency as percentage and unit output active power for a given net head in meters. The relationship between efficiency, discharge, head, and power output is expressed as follows: E =KP/HQ where: E is the efficiency, as a percentage; P is the active power; H is the height; Q is the discharge, volume/time unit; K is a constant. For example, a curve instance for a given net head could show efficiency (Y- axis) versus active power output (X-axis) or versus discharge on the X-axis.",
        "@language": "en"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
