        "@language": "en"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range": [
      {
        "@id": "http://iec.ch/TC57/CIM100#TurbineGovernorDynamics"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "http://iec.ch/TC57/CIM100#SynchronousMachineEquivalentCircuit",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment": [
      {
        "@value": "The electrical equations for all variations of the synchronous models are based on the SynchronousEquivalentCircuit diagram for the direct- and quadrature- axes. Equations for conversion between equivalent circuit and time constant reactance forms: Xd = Xad \u002B Xl X\uFFFDd = Xl \u002B Xad x Xfd / (Xad \u002B Xfd) X\uFFFDd = Xl \u002B Xad x Xfd x X1d / (Xad x Xfd \u002B Xad x X1d \u002B Xfd x X1d) Xq = Xaq \u002B Xl X\uFFFDq = Xl \u002B Xaq x X1q / (Xaq \u002B X1q) X\uFFFDq = Xl \u002B Xaq x X1q x X2q / (Xaq x X1q \u002B Xaq x X2q \u002B X1q x X2q) T\uFFFDdo = (Xad \u002B Xfd) / (omega0 x Rfd) T\uFFFDdo = (Xad x Xfd \u002B Xad x X1d \u002B Xfd x X1d) / (omega0 x R1d x (Xad \u002B Xfd) T\uFFFDqo = (Xaq \u002B X1q) / (omega0 x R1q) T\uFFFDqo = (Xaq x X1q \u002B Xaq x X2q \u002B X1q x X2q) / (omega0 x R2q x (Xaq \u002B X1q) Same equations using CIM attributes from SynchronousMachineTimeConstantReactance class on left of \u0022=\u0022 and SynchronousMachineEquivalentCircuit class on right (except as noted): xDirectSync = xad \u002B RotatingMachineDynamics.statorLeakageReactance xDirectTrans = RotatingMachineDynamics.statorLeakageReactance \u002B xad x xfd / (xad \u002B xfd) xDirectSubtrans = RotatingMachineDynamics.statorLeakageReactance \u002B xad x xfd x x1d / (xad x xfd \u002B xad x x1d \u002B xfd x x1d) xQuadSync = xaq \u002B RotatingMachineDynamics.statorLeakageReactance xQuadTrans = RotatingMachineDynamics.statorLeakageReactance \u002B xaq x x1q / (xaq\u002B x1q) xQuadSubtrans = RotatingMachineDynamics.statorLeakageReactance \u002B xaq x x1q x x2q / (xaq x x1q \u002B xaq x x2q \u002B x1q x x2q) tpdo = (xad \u002B xfd) / (2 x pi x nominal frequency x rfd) tppdo = (xad x xfd \u002B xad x x1d \u002B xfd x x1d) / (2 x pi x nominal frequency x r1d x (xad \u002B xfd) tpqo = (xaq \u002B x1q) / (2 x pi x nominal frequency x r1q) tppqo = (xaq x x1q \u002B xaq x x2q \u002B x1q x x2q) / (2 x pi x nominal frequency x r2q x (xaq \u002B x1q) These are only valid for a simplified model where \u0022Canay\u0022 reactance is zero.",
        "@language": "en"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61970.ttl"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label": [
      {
        "@value": "SynchronousMachineEquivalentCircuit",
        "@language": "en"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf": [
      {
        "@id": "http://iec.ch/TC57/CIM100#SynchronousMachineDetailed"
      }
    ],
    "https://cimbology.com/ontology/cimdoc#cimPackage": [
      {
        "@value": "IEC61970.Dynamics.StandardModels.SynchronousMachineDynamics"
      }
    ],
    "https://cimbology.com/ontology/cimdoc#packageTier": [
      {
        "@value": "Normative"
      }
    ]
  },
